## 7. INCIDENT — pytest rewrite-cache FALSE-RED (root-caused, not swept under)

After P5's sed+revert, two full-file runs showed the OSError leg RED with the
guard message — while standalone probes DENIED the 000-open 5/5 and P1..P3 had
been truthful minutes earlier. Root cause (measured, not guessed): the P5 sed
(0o000->0o644) preserves file SIZE and the mv-revert landed in the SAME WALL-
CLOCK SECOND — pytest's rewritten-bytecode cache is keyed (mtime-seconds, size),
so the stale sed'd bytecode ran while the traceback printed the REVERTED source.
Fix: purge __pycache__, sleep 1.2 s, re-run 3x GREEN, then replay the WHOLE
battery (all transcripts above are from the clean replay). Lesson recorded for
the fleet: a byte-verified revert must also invalidate bytecode caches — a
same-size same-second revert is the trap class (negative-testing: the
byte-compare passed while the EXECUTED bytes differed).

